.TH MCR-VIEW 1 "August 2026" "rusty-midnight-commander" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcr-view \- internal viewer started as mcr \-\-view
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcr
.BR \-v " | " \-\-view
.I FILE
.br
.B mcr
.BI \-\-view= FILE
.br
.B mcr
.BI \-v FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens rusty-midnight-commander's internal viewer (the
.B mcview
equivalent) on
.IR FILE .
This always uses the built-in viewer, not
.BR $PAGER .
.PP
This page is original Apache-2.0 text covering the shipped viewer CLI
and keys. It is not a copy of GNU
.BR mcview (1).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F2
Wrap / unwrap.
.TP
.B F3 / q / F10
Quit.
.TP
.B F4
Hex / text.
.TP
.B F5
Go to a line or offset.
.TP
.B F7 / /
Search.
.TP
.B n / F17
Next match.
.TP
.B F8
Parsed vs raw.
.TP
.B F9
Format / unformat (nroff-style).
.TP
.B |
Apply an external filter to the viewed bytes.
.PP
Display options cover line numbers, CR shown as ^M, wrap, and hex.
Shift+arrows extend a selection. Some compressed files are shown
through a filter. F3 from a directory panel views the highlighted
file; Shift-F3 views raw on-disk bytes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcr (1),
.BR mcr-edit (1),
.BR mcr-diff (1)
